# Keep LF in the working tree, not just in the blob.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system config, so a checkout
# there rewrites these to CRLF. Git Bash runs a CRLF script anyway, so nothing
# breaks locally and the blob stays clean — which is exactly why this goes
# unnoticed. It bites one step later: a copy taken off that checkout and onto a
# Linux box is a bash script with a \r on every line, and there it does not run.
#
# These files are the shared artefact of this repo (see STATUSLINE.md, "Same
# file on every machine"), so pin the ending rather than trusting each host's
# git config.

*.sh   text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
